	abstract = {Non-mydriatic ocular fundus photography is a promising alternative to direct ophthalmoscopy, particularly when combined with telemedicine. This review discusses these technologies from a longitudinal perspective: past, present, and future. The focus is directed to the role that nonmydriatic fundus photography and telemedicine have played in medical research and patient care, with emphasis on the major advances to date. Also discussed are the challenges to their widespread application and their substantial promise for revitalizing the importance of the ocular fundus examination in patient care, providing improved access to ophthalmic consultative services, and facilitating clinical and epidemiologic research.},
